  "unresolved": [
    "The scenario-seven summary says the alleged transactions did not exist; the detailed discussion says there was no factual basis showing that face-to-face, telephone or OTC trades existed given Gatecoin's operations. Both reject the claimed classification, but categorical nonexistence differs from evidential insufficiency. The summary also excludes that scenario from its agreement with the liquidators. The delivered text does not establish a reconciliation, a drafting error or a universal prohibition on off-platform instructions.",
    "The narrative offers a proof-based route for the later private-sale and limit-order categories where instructions preceded the change or were given without Platform use. The detailed private-sale account instead relies on subscriptions starting later and requiring Platform use, while the annexure expressly preserves an exception only for earlier limit orders. Do not silently broaden the operative exception.",
    "The earlier judgment records informed-consent and fair-dealing objections but does not adopt them as a general reason to exclude the revised terms. Individual classification needs the operative agreements, amendment mechanisms, communications, access evidence and instruction timing. Automated activity alone is insufficient, while other relevant access or use can defeat non-consenting status.",
    "Later treatment remains not checked, rather than absent. The 2025 decision develops the earlier ruling but does not establish complete current authority, an appeal outcome or freedom from subsequent distinction or displacement. Any present-law extrapolation requires a bounded subsequent-treatment inquiry.",
    "The earlier fiat discussion must be read with the express non-consenting exception and the later pooled-interest analysis. Individual-trust reasoning based on different client agreements remains a possible distinct analysis even where equivalent fungible-unit delivery produces similar results. Fungibility does not justify substitution across currencies.",
    "The court declined directions premised on assumed unidentified or uncontactable trust claimants, requiring timely claims and supporting evidence rather than automatic reservations for silent customers. Discussed statutory transfer routes, cash conversion and consent conditions were not unconditional directions. Final ETD valuation, complete sale conditions, costs apportionment and actual recoveries are not established by these extracts.",
    "A provider-specific transfer requires contracts and governing law linking token title, beneficial interests and underlying product rights; identified assets and beneficiaries; custody and delegation arrangements; funding and mandates; assent evidence; settlement finality; and records addressing conflicts and encumbrances. Tokens that aim to represent ownership and disclosures describing ownership do not themselves create enforceable rights.",
    "For regulatory fulfilment, assess actual operational soundness, record accuracy, compatibility, smart-contract integrity, cybersecurity, privacy, recovery and business continuity, including discrepancies and remediation. Public-permissionless networks require additional proper controls, not a categorical prohibition. The precise grammatical reach of the SFC-satisfaction language and the missing explanatory footnotes remain qualified.",
    "Where the provider also acts as an intermediary, issuer-side responsibility despite outsourcing differs from due diligence on issuers and vendors and satisfaction with their controls before investment-related activities. The supplied Appendix addresses enforceability, settlement finality, reconciliation and custody; its extraction disagreement remains unresolved. Its omnibus exception concerns other customers' assets, not the custodian's own assets.",
    "Primary dealing remains subject to underlying authorisation requirements and tokenisation safeguards. Secondary trading has distinct pricing, orderly-trading, liquidity, disclosure and incorporated requirements whose complete substance is not delivered. Self-distribution entails applicable intermediary, onboarding and suitability duties; competence must be confirmed. Prior consultation and potentially required approval are distinct. Actual applicability, consultation, approvals and performance remain unknown."
